on of ALL native field IDs (including hidden), obtained from detail.fields; add fields first then reorder separately. Reordering preserves identities/filters and never requires ClearFields. Native title stays attached to the schedule; do not replace it with detached sheet text. For bounded fieldFormats-only edits, use an exact scheduleId and unique native field names with heading, widthFeet, hidden, horizontalAlignment and/or headingOrientation. Separate native readback requires before/after field definitions, unchanged bindings, unrequested attributes and collateral schedule fingerprints; mixed structural/color edits remain unverified by this checker. Inspect enlarged rendering and revise supported differences; do not repeat an uncertain mutation. For automatic separate host readback of these defaults/order, send an exact scheduleId with only fieldOrder and/or appearance text-type IDs plus showTitle/showHeaders; apply other configuration in separate bounded calls. The host independently reads requested native defaults/order and requires preservation fingerprints plus native dependency proof before accepting a wider native change inventory. Incomplete or unexplained scope stays unverified. This does not prove whole-sheet layout or engineering. Check fresh detail and enlarged rendering after changes. Apply advanced regular-schedule configuration (isItemized=false groups matching instances into summary rows; sort/group by type and airflow to keep different flows separate): fields, calculated fields/formulas, filters, sort/group, conditional formatting, field styling, appearance, filter-by-sheet, column widths, and row heights. Body: {scheduleId?|query?,addFields?,fieldOrder?,calculatedFields?,filters?,sortGroup?,showGrandTotals?,isItemized?,columnWidths?,rowHeights?,fieldFormats?,conditionalFormats?,appearance?,filterBySheet?,replaceFilters?,replaceSortGroup?,dryRun?}.",
